==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|en|la|sorōricīdium||killing of one’s sister}}, from {{m|la|soror||sister}} + {{m|la|-cīdium||killing}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|en|la:soror|t1=sister|cide|id2=killing|t2=killing}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-sororicide.wav|a=US}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[killing]] of one's [[sister]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Albert Lee Strickland|chapter=Familicide|editor=Michael John Brennan|title=The A–Z of Death and Dying: Social, Medical, and Cultural Aspects|location=Santa Barbara, Calif.|publisher=w:Greenwood Publishing Group|year=2014|pages=205–206|isbn=978-1-4408-0344-4|passage=Terms related to familicide include filicide (the killing of one's child or children), uxoricide (the killing of one's wife), fratricide or '''sororicide''' (the killing of one's brother or sister), avunculicide (the killing of one's uncle), and nepoticide (the killing of one's nephew).}}

